    "number": "Theorem 4",
    "quote": "Consider the semiparametric contextual bandit problem under \\pref{as:env} and~\\pref{as:bd}. For any parameter $\\delta \\in (0,1)$, with probability at least $1-\\delta$, \\pref{alg:pseudocode} has regret at most $O(d\\sqrt{T} \\log(T/\\delta))$."
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Regret defined as sum_t <theta, z_{t,a*_t} - z_{t,a_t}> (realized actions), bounded w.p. 1-delta. Proof gives the finer O(d sqrt(T) log T + sqrt(dT log T log(T/delta)) + sqrt(T log(T/delta) log(1/delta))). Two-action case sketch gives O(sqrt(Td log(T/delta) log(T/d)) + d sqrt(T) log(T/d)). Bound independent of number of actions K. Per-round convex feasibility problem (Lemma 8), so polynomial in K and d."
  },
